IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc6-smp`
IMPORT `ssc6-ssp`

-- Tests for ssc6-ssp.l4 (Part XI, ss 151-163).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the Act's text (ukpga-1992-4.txt, lines 3095-3240),
-- beside the assertion. None is copied from what the code printed.
-- Arbitrary dates: 1 January 2026 is a Thursday; 4 January 2026 is a Sunday.

§ `Tests for Part XI`

§§ `Sunday`

-- s 154(3), s 157(3) and s 171(1A) speak of a week "beginning with Sunday".
#ASSERT (Day (Date 4 1 2026)) MODULO 7 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 151(4) -- a day of incapacity for work`

-- Arguments: incapable by reason of a specific disease or disablement; deemed so by regulations.
#ASSERT `s 151(4) the day is a day of incapacity for work in relation to the contract of service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 151(4) the day is a day of incapacity for work in relation to the contract of service` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 151(4) the day is a day of incapacity for work in relation to the contract of service` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 151(4) the day is a day of incapacity for work in relation to the contract of service` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 151(1) -- the employer's liability for a day`

#ASSERT `s 151(1) the employer is liable to make a payment of statutory sick pay in respect of the day` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 151(1) the employer is liable to make a payment of statutory sick pay in respect of the day` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 151(1) the employer is liable to make a payment of statutory sick pay in respect of the day` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 151(1) the employer is liable to make a payment of statutory sick pay in respect of the day` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 151(1) the employer is liable to make a payment of statutory sick pay in respect of the day` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 151(1) the employer is liable to make a payment of statutory sick pay in respect of the day` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 151(1) the employer is liable to make a payment of statutory sick pay in respect of the day` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 151(1) the employer is liable to make a payment of statutory sick pay in respect of the day` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 151(2), (3) -- void agreements`

#ASSERT `s 151(2) the agreement is void to the extent that it purports` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 151(2) the agreement is void to the extent that it purports` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 151(2) the agreement is void to the extent that it purports` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: the agreement authorises deductions; authorised to make the same deductions from contractual pay; would be so authorised.
#ASSERT `s 151(3) the agreement is protected from being void by virtue of subsection (2)(a)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 151(3) the agreement is protected from being void by virtue of subsection (2)(a)` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 151(3) the agreement is protected from being void by virtue of subsection (2)(a)` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 151(3) the agreement is protected from being void by virtue of subsection (2)(a)` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 151(5), (6) -- more than one contract; who pays`

-- Arguments: more than one contract of service with the same employer; the case is prescribed.
#ASSERT `s 151(5) the employer is treated as a different employer in relation to each contract of service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 151(5) the employer is treated as a different employer in relation to each contract of service` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 151(5) the employer is treated as a different employer in relation to each contract of service` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 151(5) the employer is treated as a different employer in relation to each contract of service` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 151(6) who is liable to make payments of statutory sick pay` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST `s 151 the Commissioners of Inland Revenue`
#ASSERT `s 151(6) who is liable to make payments of statutory sick pay` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST `s 151 the employer`
#ASSERT `s 151(6) who is liable to make payments of statutory sick pay` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 152 -- period of incapacity for work`

#ASSERT `s 152(3) the number of weeks specified in the Act` EQUALS 8
-- Arguments: days in the stretch (every day of the week counted); how many of them are days of incapacity.
#ASSERT `s 152(2) the days form a period of incapacity for work` 1 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 152(2) the days form a period of incapacity for work` 7 7 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 152(2) the days form a period of incapacity for work` 7 6 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 152(2) the days form a period of incapacity for work` 2 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 152(2) the days form a period of incapacity for work` 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 152(5): no day of the week is disregarded, so Saturday and Sunday count.
#ASSERT `s 152(5) the number of days in the period counting every day of the week` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 152(5) the number of days in the period counting every day of the week` (Date 2 1 2026) (Date 4 1 2026) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `s 152(5) the number of days in the period counting every day of the week` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 7 1 2026) EQUALS 7
-- s 152(3): earlier period ends Thursday 1 January 2026. "Not more than 8 weeks" (56 days) between: a later
-- period starting 27 February 2026 has 56 days strictly between (2 January to 26 February); 28 February has 57.
#ASSERT `s 152(3) the two periods of incapacity for work are treated as a single period` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 27 2 2026) 8 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 152(3) the two periods of incapacity for work are treated as a single period` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 28 2 2026) 8 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 152(3) the two periods of incapacity for work are treated as a single period` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 2 1 2026) 8 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 152(3) the two periods of incapacity for work are treated as a single period` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 8 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 152(3) the two periods of incapacity for work are treated as a single period` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2025) 8 EQUALS NOTHING
-- if regulations under subsection (4) substituted 9 weeks (63 days), 28 February would be within it
#ASSERT `s 152(3) the two periods of incapacity for work are treated as a single period` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 28 2 2026) 9 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Arguments: before the contract was made or after it ended; not a day the contract required him to be available.
#ASSERT `s 152(6) the day may be a day of incapacity for work notwithstanding` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 152(6) the day may be a day of incapacity for work notwithstanding` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 152(6) the day may be a day of incapacity for work notwithstanding` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 153 -- period of entitlement`

-- limb (d) and subsection (11). Arguments: is, or has been, pregnant; the pregnancy terminated before the disqualifying period otherwise than by confinement.
#ASSERT `s 153(2)(d) the period of entitlement ends on the day before the disqualifying period` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 153(2)(d) the period of entitlement ends on the day before the disqualifying period` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 153(2)(d) the period of entitlement ends on the day before the disqualifying period` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153(2)(d) the period of entitlement ends on the day before the disqualifying period` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- the end: whichever of the four first occurs. Arguments: last day of the period of incapacity; day maximum entitlement reached;
-- day the contract ends; day before the disqualifying period; limb (d) applies.
#ASSERT `s 153(2) the period of entitlement ends on` (JUST (Date 31 1 2026)) (JUST (Date 15 1 2026)) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 153(2) the period of entitlement ends on` (JUST (Date 31 1 2026)) (JUST (Date 15 1 2026)) (JUST (Date 10 1 2026)) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 153(2) the period of entitlement ends on` (JUST (Date 8 1 2026)) (JUST (Date 15 1 2026)) (JUST (Date 10 1 2026)) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 8 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 153(2) the period of entitlement ends on` (JUST (Date 31 1 2026)) (JUST (Date 15 1 2026)) NOTHING (JUST (Date 5 1 2026)) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST (Date 5 1 2026)
-- limb (d) does not apply, so its day is ignored
#ASSERT `s 153(2) the period of entitlement ends on` (JUST (Date 31 1 2026)) (JUST (Date 15 1 2026)) NOTHING (JUST (Date 5 1 2026)) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2026)
-- whether limb (d) applies is unanswered and it has a day: the end is not covered
#ASSERT `s 153(2) the period of entitlement ends on` (JUST (Date 31 1 2026)) (JUST (Date 15 1 2026)) NOTHING (JUST (Date 5 1 2026)) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- unanswered and no day for it: the other limbs decide
#ASSERT `s 153(2) the period of entitlement ends on` (JUST (Date 31 1 2026)) (JUST (Date 15 1 2026)) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2026)
-- nothing has happened yet: the period of entitlement has not ended
#ASSERT `s 153(2) the period of entitlement ends on` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 153(2) the period of entitlement ends on` (JUST (Date 31 1 2026)) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)
-- the same day twice
#ASSERT `s 153(2) the period of entitlement ends on` (JUST (Date 15 1 2026)) (JUST (Date 15 1 2026)) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2026)
-- the beginning. Arguments: first day of the period of incapacity; the day the contract first takes effect; subsection (9) applies;
-- the first day the earnings attract secondary Class 1 liability; that day falls within a period of incapacity; falls between two periods treated as one; first day of the second.
#ASSERT `s 153(7) the period of entitlement begins on` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) FALSE (Date 25 1 2026) TRUE FALSE (Date 15 2 2026) EQUALS Date 20 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 153(7) the period of entitlement begins on` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) TRUE (Date 25 1 2026) TRUE FALSE (Date 15 2 2026) EQUALS Date 25 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 153(7) the period of entitlement begins on` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) FALSE (Date 25 1 2026) FALSE TRUE (Date 15 2 2026) EQUALS Date 15 2 2026
#ASSERT `s 153(7) the period of entitlement begins on` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) FALSE (Date 25 1 2026) FALSE FALSE (Date 15 2 2026) EQUALS Date 1 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 153(7) the period of entitlement begins on` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) TRUE (Date 25 1 2026) FALSE FALSE (Date 15 2 2026) EQUALS Date 1 1 2026
-- the first condition: the day falls within a period of entitlement. Arguments: the day; the period; Schedule 11 prevents a period arising.
#ASSERT `s 153(1) the first condition is satisfied` (Date 10 1 2026) (`s 153 Period of entitlement` WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 153(1) the first condition is satisfied` (Date 1 1 2026) (`s 153 Period of entitlement` WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 153(1) the first condition is satisfied` (Date 31 1 2026) (`s 153 Period of entitlement` WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 153(1) the first condition is satisfied` (Date 1 2 2026) (`s 153 Period of entitlement` WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153(1) the first condition is satisfied` (Date 31 12 2025) (`s 153 Period of entitlement` WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a period of entitlement that has not ended has no last day
#ASSERT `s 153(1) the first condition is satisfied` (Date 1 2 2026) (`s 153 Period of entitlement` WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS NOTHING) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 153(1) the first condition is satisfied` (Date 1 2 2026) (`s 153 Period of entitlement` WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS NOTHING) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153(1) the first condition is satisfied` (Date 10 1 2026) (`s 153 Period of entitlement` WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 153(4) the period is also a period of entitlement as between the employee and another employer` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 153(4) the period is also a period of entitlement as between the employee and another employer` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 153(12) -- the terms it defines`

-- "confinement" is s 171(1)'s.
#ASSERT `s 153(12) she has been confined` (Labour OF 40, TRUE, Date 10 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 153(12) she has been confined` (Labour OF 24, FALSE, Date 10 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "disqualifying period": for SMP, the maternity pay period 1 January to 31 December 2026; for MA, the maternity allowance period 1 June to 30 November 2027.
-- Arguments: the relevant date; entitled to SMP; entitled to MA; the maternity pay period; the maternity allowance period.
#ASSERT `s 153(12) the relevant date falls within the disqualifying period` (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE FALSE (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2026) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 6 2027, `the last day` IS Date 30 11 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 153(12) the relevant date falls within the disqualifying period` (Date 31 12 2026) TRUE FALSE (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2026) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 6 2027, `the last day` IS Date 30 11 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 153(12) the relevant date falls within the disqualifying period` (Date 31 12 2025) TRUE FALSE (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2026) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 6 2027, `the last day` IS Date 30 11 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153(12) the relevant date falls within the disqualifying period` (Date 1 1 2027) TRUE FALSE (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2026) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 6 2027, `the last day` IS Date 30 11 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153(12) the relevant date falls within the disqualifying period` (Date 1 6 2027) FALSE TRUE (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2026) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 6 2027, `the last day` IS Date 30 11 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 153(12) the relevant date falls within the disqualifying period` (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE TRUE (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2026) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 6 2027, `the last day` IS Date 30 11 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153(12) the relevant date falls within the disqualifying period` (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE TRUE (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2026) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 6 2027, `the last day` IS Date 30 11 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 153(12) the relevant date falls within the disqualifying period` (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE FALSE (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2026) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 6 2027, `the last day` IS Date 30 11 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 153(12) the maternity allowance period` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 6 2027, `the last day` IS Date 30 11 2027) EQUALS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 6 2027, `the last day` IS Date 30 11 2027
#ASSERT `s 153(12) the maternity pay period` (Date 1 1 2026) 39 EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 30 9 2026)
#ASSERT `s 153(12) the maternity pay period` (Date 1 1 2026) 53 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 154 -- qualifying days`

-- Arguments: agreement on which days; the day is one agreed; regulations determine the day to be a qualifying day.
#ASSERT `s 154(2) the day is a qualifying day` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 154(2) the day is a qualifying day` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 154(2) the day is a qualifying day` FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 154(2) the day is a qualifying day` FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 154(2) the day is a qualifying day` FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 154(1) the second condition is satisfied` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 154(1) the second condition is satisfied` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 154(1) the second condition is satisfied` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 154(3) the agreement provides at least one qualifying day in the week` 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 154(3) the agreement provides at least one qualifying day in the week` 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 154(3) the agreement provides at least one qualifying day in the week` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 154(4) the day is also a qualifying day as between the employee and another employer` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 154(4) the day is also a qualifying day as between the employee and another employer` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 155 -- limitations on entitlement`

-- 28 times the weekly rate: at the Act's own rate of 123.25 that is 3,451; at 100 it is 2,800.
#ASSERT `s 155(4) the number of times the weekly rate that makes up the entitlement limit` EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `s 155(4) the entitlement limit in pounds` 100 EQUALS 2800
#ASSERT `s 155(4) the entitlement limit in pounds` 123.25 EQUALS 3451
#ASSERT `s 155(4) the entitlement limit in pounds` 0 EQUALS 0
-- s 155(3): "first reaches or passes". Arguments: the limit; the amount before the first of these days; the first of these days; the daily amounts.
#ASSERT `s 155(3) the day on which the maximum entitlement is reached` 10 0 (Date 1 1 2026) (LIST 4, 4, 4, 4) EQUALS JUST (Date 3 1 2026)
-- reaches: 5 + 5 = 10 on the second day
#ASSERT `s 155(3) the day on which the maximum entitlement is reached` 10 0 (Date 1 1 2026) (LIST 5, 5, 5) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 1 2026)
-- passes: 7 + 7 = 14 on the second day
#ASSERT `s 155(3) the day on which the maximum entitlement is reached` 10 0 (Date 1 1 2026) (LIST 7, 7) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 1 2026)
-- one short on the last day it is not reached
#ASSERT `s 155(3) the day on which the maximum entitlement is reached` 10 0 (Date 1 1 2026) (LIST 4, 5) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 155(3) the day on which the maximum entitlement is reached` 100 0 (Date 1 1 2026) (LIST 4, 4, 4, 4) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 155(3) the day on which the maximum entitlement is reached` 10 0 (Date 1 1 2026) EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
-- an amount already entitled to before these days counts
#ASSERT `s 155(3) the day on which the maximum entitlement is reached` 10 8 (Date 1 1 2026) (LIST 2, 2) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 155(3) the day on which the maximum entitlement is reached` 10 8 (Date 1 1 2026) (LIST 1, 1) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 1 2026)
-- s 155(2): an excess is barred; otherwise the subsection says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 155(2) the employee is entitled as against the employer to the aggregate amount` 3451.01 3451 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 155(2) the employee is entitled as against the employer to the aggregate amount` 3451 3451 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 155(2) the employee is entitled as against the employer to the aggregate amount` 100 3451 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 156 -- notification`

-- Arguments: the employer would otherwise be liable for the qualifying day; the employer has not been duly notified of the day.
#ASSERT `s 156(2) the employer is entitled to withhold payment for the day` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 156(2) the employer is entitled to withhold payment for the day` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 156(2) the employer is entitled to withhold payment for the day` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 156(2) the employer is entitled to withhold payment for the day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 156(3)(a) the period of entitlement is affected by the withholding` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 156(3)(a) the period of entitlement is affected by the withholding` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: the amount for the day; the employer withholds it.
#ASSERT `s 156(3)(b) the amount counted towards the maximum entitlement in pounds` 24.65 TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 156(3)(b) the amount counted towards the maximum entitlement in pounds` 24.65 FALSE EQUALS 24.65

§§ `s 157 -- rates`

-- The Act: the lower of 123.25 and 80% of normal weekly earnings. They cross at 123.25 / 0.8 = 154.0625.
#ASSERT `s 157(1)(a) the weekly rate cap in pounds` EQUALS 123.25
#ASSERT `s 157(1)(b) the percentage of normal weekly earnings` EQUALS 0.8
#ASSERT `s 157(1) the weekly rate of statutory sick pay in pounds` 100 EQUALS 80
#ASSERT `s 157(1) the weekly rate of statutory sick pay in pounds` 154.06 EQUALS 123.248
#ASSERT `s 157(1) the weekly rate of statutory sick pay in pounds` 154.0625 EQUALS 123.25
#ASSERT `s 157(1) the weekly rate of statutory sick pay in pounds` 154.07 EQUALS 123.25
#ASSERT `s 157(1) the weekly rate of statutory sick pay in pounds` 500 EQUALS 123.25
#ASSERT `s 157(1) the weekly rate of statutory sick pay in pounds` 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 157(1) the weekly rate of statutory sick pay specified in section 157(1) in pounds` EQUALS 123.25
-- s 157(3): the weekly rate divided by the qualifying days in the week.
#ASSERT `s 157(3) the amount of statutory sick pay payable in respect of the day in pounds` 123.25 5 EQUALS JUST 24.65
#ASSERT `s 157(3) the amount of statutory sick pay payable in respect of the day in pounds` 123.25 1 EQUALS JUST 123.25
#ASSERT `s 157(3) the amount of statutory sick pay payable in respect of the day in pounds` 140 7 EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `s 157(3) the amount of statutory sick pay payable in respect of the day in pounds` 100 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 159A, s 160, s 161, s 162`

#ASSERT `s 159A(3) the payment is a contributions payment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 159A(3) the payment is a contributions payment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 159A(3) the payment is a contributions payment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
